<%#
  The thread and the box to add to it.

  Subscribed to the guest stream, so an answer written by the bot in a
  background job or by a person in the portal arrives on this page without the
  guest touching anything. Only once there is a conversation to subscribe to --
  a visitor who has not written yet has no thread of their own.

  Wrapped in one region with a stable id because that is what a send replaces.
  The first message is the case that decides the shape: until it exists there is
  no thread to subscribe to, so the reply to a send has to be able to hand the
  page its subscription, its log and its box together.
%>
<%= tag.div(id: PublicUI::Chat::Panel::REGION_ID) do %>
  <% if conversation %>
    <%= turbo_stream_from conversation, :guest %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render PublicUI::Chat::Panel.new do |panel| %>
    <% panel.with_header(title: hotel.name, subtitle: concierge_chat_header_subtitle(conversation, hotel)) %>
    <% panel.with_log(messages: messages, hotel: hotel) %>
    <% panel.with_notice(**concierge_chat_notice(conversation, hotel)) %>
    <% panel.with_composer(url: concierge_chat_messages_path(hotel)) %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
